WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.670
Oh good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:06.089
I didn't see you there, I was busy working
on my new book in my usual novel writing position.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.870
Anyway, today's video comes to you in 4 parts.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.610
Part 1: Johning
So the nice people at The Hollywood Reporter

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:15.050
wrote an article about The Fault In Our Stars
movie and me, and they included this picture,

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.410
and then long-time nerdfighter Emily posted
a picture of herself doing what she called

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:19.410
"johning".

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.390
And then Charlie McDonnell did one, and then
began a massive flood of johning including

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.919
Josh Sundquist, and this very small person,
and you, Hank and lots, and lots of other

00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:29.919
people.

00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:32.610
Anyway Hank, the cast of the movie thinks
that johning is hilarious, as do I, so I just

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.080
wanted to say, thank you for johning.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.380
Part 2: Your birthday!

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.950
Hank it was your birthday yesterday.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.170
Happy Birthday!

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.910
Unlike last year I did remember to get you
a present this year from me and also from

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:43.910
nerdfighteria.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.120
The original arcade game, Teenage Mutant Ninja
Turtles.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.940
TMNT for life, Hank!

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.860
This is a real tattoo by the way, is that
weird?

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.080
*whispers* It's not a real tattoo.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.260
Also Hank, I got you a donation to Partners
in Health.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.460
Partners in Health, for actual life.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.870
Part 3: Hank Green and the Perfect Strangers
It just occurred to me that this video is

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.940
going to have more than 3 parts.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:01.940
I apologize for that.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.540
Why does my hair look so like weird and grown
up and professional?

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.240
Hank, your excellent new album Incongruent
comes out tomorrow, so nerdfighters, that

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.570
means that today is the last day that you
can pre-order a signed copy.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.280
There is a link in the doobly-doo.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.369
Also, for those of you who prefer your goods
and services digitally, the album will be

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:18.880
out on iTunes tomorrow.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.359
Hank, I don't want to get all Esther Day-y
on you or anything, but when I was listening

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:26.229
to the album, I was reminded of what a great
musician you are in addition to all the other

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:30.369
things you do, and I really admire you and
the way that you go about your work.

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:31.510
I'm getting Esther Day-y.

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.130
Anyway Hank, long story short, you're not
that cool, you're a grapefruit.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.889
Part 4: The many headless and/or faceless
people in my hotel room

00:01:36.889 --> 00:01:39.929
So Hank I'm doing all this like TFiOS press
junket stuff with the cast of the movie and

00:01:39.929 --> 00:01:44.229
they put us in a very nice hotel, but there
are a lot of people in my room with no heads.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.590
This person has no head.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.049
This person has no head.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:48.920
This person, also no head.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.920
No head.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.719
And then there are these people who I think
have heads but definitely do not have faces.

00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:57.299
This guy has half a face which by the standards
of this hotel room puts him in like the top

00:01:57.299 --> 00:01:58.479
1% of facedness.

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:01.060
Part 5: Tour
So Hank, the Fault In Our Stars movie stuff

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.100
is starting to like actually happen now.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:07.040
Like we just had our first screening for fans
of the book, which was nuts!

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.420
And most importantly, they liked the movie.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.230
Like Hank, I guess I want the movie to do
well, but to be completely honest with you,

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:16.790
ultimately what I want is for people who care
about the book a lot to like the movie.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.230
And I got to sit in the back of the theatre
for like the last fifteen minutes of the movie

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.170
and I heard quite a lot of sobbing, which
I found very encouraging.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:27.129
Anyway, now, starting today actually, I get
to go on tour with Shailene and Ansel and

00:02:27.129 --> 00:02:28.129
Nat.

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:30.870
Okay for of these the doors will open at 5,
and the show will start around 6:30.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:35.129
This is Fox's tour, not mine, so I seriously
have no idea what's going to happen but I

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:36.720
do know that it's free!

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.110
Today, we will be in Miami, Florida at the
Dolphin Mall.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.290
Is it an actual dolphin?

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.110
Is it a gigantic dolphin that they turned
into a mall?

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.530
That seems like animal cruelty.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.370
Wednesday, we will be in Cleveland at the
Tower City Center.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.110
Thursday, we will be in lovely Nashville,
Tennessee at the War Memorial Auditorium at

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:55.560
the Tennessee Performing Arts Center, and
Friday, May 9th we'll be in Dallas, Texas

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.709
at the South Side Ballroom at Gilley's, or
possibly Jilley's.

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:01.920
Like I said earlier, I don't know much about
what's gonna actually happen at these events,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.230
but I know there won't be signings because
they're just expecting a lot of people.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.390
But there will be like Q&amp;A and general merriment.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:08.560
I think it'll be a lot of fun.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.010
Hank, congratulations again on your great
album and thank you for being such a good

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:16.650
friend and brother to me in this great but
also very weird time of my life.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.930
DFTBA, Nerdfighteria!

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.090
Hank, I will see you on Friday.

